  "body": "Part of #748.\n\n#748's first PR (the `cargo xtask` crate, `issue/748-xtask-gate`) ports the gate (`gate.ps1` / `gate.sh`) and `collect-decisions.*` into `cargo xtask gate ...` / `cargo xtask decisions ...`. It leaves `scripts/release.ps1` as it is. That script is 243 lines in 10 phases (preflight, gate, version bump in Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, commit, build, zip staging that mirrors `.github/workflows/release.yml`, signing through `sign.ps1`, the Inno Setup installer through `installer.ps1`, tag / `-NoTag`) and doesn't port cleanly in the same PR.\n\nToday a cut can only run on Windows.\n\nProposal: `cargo xtask release --version X.Y.Z [--no-tag] [--skip-gate] [--skip-build] [--installer] [--dry-run]` takes the platform-neutral phases: preflight, gate (`cargo xtask gate release`), version bump, commit, release build and zip staging. The packaging steps run per OS (`installer.ps1` / `sign.ps1` on Windows, `package-*.sh` on macOS / Linux), and a step the OS can't run is refused by name. `scripts/release.ps1` becomes a thin wrapper. AGENTS.md release step 2 then names `cargo xtask release`.\n\nDone means: `cargo xtask release --version X.Y.Z --no-tag --dry-run` prints the same phases as `scripts/release.ps1 -DryRun -NoTag` on Windows, and runs (or refuses by name) on macOS and Linux. Unit tests pin the version bump and the zip layout. `release.ps1` is a wrapper. #748 closes with this.\n",
